p=A.ar(["Stripe Integration","Implementing Stripe API for secure payment processing","PayPal Integration","Integrating PayPal for seamless online transactions",f,"Ensures a well-organized and maintainable codebase for easy scalability","GetIt","For Dependency Injection and managing Singletons across the app",a3,"State management using Cubit for handling payment processes","Dartz","Using Either for managing success and failure states in payment processes","GoRouter","Routing between payment screens and managing app navigation","DIO","Using Dio for handling API requests with error handling during payment gateway communication","Postman","For API testing and ensuring successful communication with Stripe and PayPal APIs"],b1,b1)
p=A.px("The Simple Payment App Stripe & PayPal demonstrates the integration of popular payment gateways, focusing on Stripe and PayPal, in a Flutter application. Built with clean architecture and the MVVM pattern, this app ensures a well-structured, maintainable codebase. It uses Dio for API communication, dartz for robust error handling, and GoRouter for seamless navigation between pages.This app provides a hands-on approach to understanding the differences between payment gateways and in-app purchases, choosing the right gateway for specific needs, and implementing payment solutions efficiently. It is an ideal project for learning practical integration techniques, exploring payment gateway features, and mastering essential Flutter packages like Cubit for state management and GetIt for dependency injection.","assets/images/payment_app/image.png",!1,A.pv(A.b(["assets/images/payment_app/image1.png","assets/images/payment_app/image2.png","assets/images/payment_app/image3.png","assets/images/payment_app/image4.png","assets/images/payment_app/image5.png","assets/images/payment_app/image6.png"],b3),"Learning Purpose - Integrate Payment methods in apps Stripe & PayPal",p,"assets/videos/payment_app/payment_app.mp4"),"https://github.com/HassanMadkour/Payment-Feature","Simple Payment App Stripe & PayPal")
o=A.ar(["Responsive Widgets","Expanded, Flexible, Spacer, FittedBox, SingleScrollView, CustomScrollView, LayoutBuilder, AspectRatio and others","MediaQuery","To get size of screen such as height , width  and so on","Responsive Text","create function to return responsive text size Depend on size of screen"],b1,b1)
o=A.px("A versatile and highly adaptive dashboard application designed to provide an optimal user experience across various screen sizes, from mobile to tablet and desktop. This project utilizes a variety of responsive and adaptive widgets, including Expanded, Flexible, Spacer, FittedBox, and LayoutBuilder, along with MediaQuery for screen size detection. It also includes a custom function for responsive text scaling, ensuring clarity and readability on all devices. Developed as a learning project, this app serves as a comprehensive example of building RESPONSIVE & ADAPTIVE applications in Flutter.",a4,!1,A.pv(A.b(["assets/images/responsive_dashboard/image1.png","assets/images/responsive_dashboard/image2.png","assets/images/responsive_dashboard/image3.png","assets/images/responsive_dashboard/image4.png","assets/images/responsive_dashboard/image5.png",a4],b3),"Learning Purpose - Creating RESPONSIVE & ADAPTIVE application for mobile , tablet and desktop ",o,"assets/videos/responsive_dashboard/Responsive_app.mp4"),"https://github.com/HassanMadkour/Responsive-Dashboard","Responsive Dashboard App")
n=A.ar([f,"Good files and folder structure","MVVM Pattern","Model view view model with Cubit as Manager","GetIt"," for Dependency Injection and SingleTon",a3,a5,"Dartz","using Either to return success and failure","Pagination","apply pagination to requests to improve app","Splash Screen","create Splash Screen for app with simple animation","GoRouter","Package to route among pages","DIO",a6,"Postman ","for API testing"],b1,b1)
n=A.px("The Simple Book App allows users to browse a selection of books, retrieve details, and read descriptions by integrating a RESTful API. Built with a clean architecture and the MVVM pattern, this app demonstrates effective file organization, dependency injection with GetIt, and state management using Cubit. The use of Dio for API handling, alongside dartz for error management, ensures smooth data flow and reliable error handling, making this app a well-structured, learning-focused project.",a7,!1,A.pv(A.b([a7,"assets/images/book_app/image2.png","assets/images/book_app/image3.png","assets/images/book_app/image4.png"],b3),"Learning Purpose - Clean Architecture & MVVM Pattern",n,"assets/videos/book_app/book_app.mp4"),"https://github.com/HassanMadkour/Book-App","Simple Book App")
m=A.ar(["Hive ","For storage in phone cache","cubit","As state Management"],b1,b1)
m=A.px("The Simple Note App is a basic note-taking application developed to explore local storage in Flutter. Built with Hive for efficient offline storage, the app enables users to save, edit, and delete notes without relying on an external database, making it lightweight and fast.",a8,!1,A.pv(A.b([a8,"assets/images/note_app/image2.png","assets/images/note_app/image3.png"],b3),"Learning Purpose - Local Storage Using Hive",m,"assets/videos/note_app/note_app.mp4"),"https://github.com/HassanMadkour/Note-App","Simple Note App")
